      "id": 1,
      "text": "Mutual was settled after the Cherokee Outlet Land Run in September 1893, which opened the region for non-Native American homesteading.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/mutual_oklahoma"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "A post office named Mutual was established on June 4, 1895, with Elias Heckart serving as the first postmaster.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/mutual_oklahoma"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Mutual officially incorporated as a town in 1908.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mutual%2C_Oklahoma"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "By 1910, Mutual featured two churches, a bank, a feed mill, a machine shop, and a hotel.",
